  "term": "refractive index",
  "definition": "Refractive index is an optical property describing how hemoglobin behaves with light. In this packet, it is treated as a value that changes with wavelength, concentration, and whether hemoglobin is oxygenated or deoxygenated, which matters for optical diagnostic methods.",
